#!/bin/bash
# Orca Slicer's WebKit setup wizard paints a blank page unless its Flatpak is
# started with the software compositing and DMA-BUF renderer paths disabled
# (#423). Apply that pair once per account, to Orca only.
set -euo pipefail

flatpak_binary=${SPACED_FLATPAK_REAL:-/usr/bin/flatpak}
state_dir=${SPACED_APP_STATE_DIR:-${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/spaced}
marker="$state_dir/flatpak-app-env-11.26.3"

[ ! -e "$marker" ] || exit 0
# No Flatpak command yet: leave the marker unwritten so a later login can still
# apply the override. This costs no fork and touches no application.
[ -x "$flatpak_binary" ] || exit 0

# Record completion only after success. A temporary failure must not leave an
# account permanently without the workaround; retry on the next login/install.
mkdir -p "$state_dir"

if ! "$flatpak_binary" override --user \
    --env=WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE=1 \
    --env=WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1 \
    com.orcaslicer.OrcaSlicer; then
    logger -t spaced-flatpak-app-env \
        "Could not set the WebKit overrides for com.orcaslicer.OrcaSlicer" || true
    exit 1
fi
touch "$marker"
